Figma Make — Interactive High-Fidelity Prototype
https://www.figma.com/make/zyY5RWn0jxdGemyINQ5WW8/One-Page-Infographic-Design?t=gE0yu2vt4PIk53aB-1&preview-route=%2Fsearch

The final, clickable high-fidelity prototype of HuskyFind, built and refined using Figma Make and broken down step by step through 
the full user flow: splash/login → home → search (by category, building, or keyword) → item details → in-app messaging with the finder
→ claimed status. The prototype reflects every change that came out of usability testing, including the privacy-protecting messaging 
system (no personal contact info required to connect), the AI Privacy Scan that blurs sensitive details on posted photos, and a 
confirmation screen that gives users clear feedback after posting or messaging. It's the most complete, "ready to use" version of the 
four design iterations the project went through, from the earliest low-fidelity sketches to this final build.
